 Securing Vault with TLS
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Install and configure HashiCorp Vault on a Linux system
Generate and configure TLS certificates for Vault encryption
Set up Vault with TLS encryption to secure data in transit
Implement mutual TLS (mTLS) authentication for enhanced security
Verify TLS and mTLS configurations are working correctly
Understand the importance of certificate-based security in production environments
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with file permissions and directory structures
Basic knowledge of PKI (Public Key Infrastructure) concepts
Understanding of TLS/SSL fundamentals
Basic knowledge of JSON configuration files
